{
 "summary": "Expands the `ipc` fuzz target to test bidirectional communication through client callbacks and validate server-side argument deserialization before values return over the pipe. It also sends arbitrary raw Cap'n Proto request and response payloads for `CTransaction` and `UniValue` to test error handling when deserializing malformed data directly in `libmultiprocess` clients and servers.",
 "problem": "The initial IPC fuzz target only tested round-trip calls where data was serialized by `libmultiprocess` before being deserialized, meaning corrupted or malformed payloads were not tested against client/server deserializers, reverse callback channels were unexercised, and serialization errors on the client-to-server path could be masked during the return trip.",
 "evidence": [
  "Addresses reviewer feedback from #35118 suggesting server-side assertions on incoming arguments to detect one-way serialization mismatches.",
  "Follows up on multiprocess fuzzing roadmap in #23015 by testing raw input deserialization and bidirectional callback support."
 ],
